    <region left="355" top="3474" width="417" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Converter current margin at the 58% brightness limit</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="3537" width="773" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> 58% is the highest brightness that keeps the theoretical 5 V load within the converter’s 5 A rating, leaving a margin of only about 0.04 A. It is therefore treated as an upper brightness limit set in software. The measured maximum current below (2.91 A, safety factor ≈ 1.72) shows a much larger margin in practice, because not all LEDs run at full white simultaneously.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="3600" width="184" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Measured Converter Current</p>
