    <region left="333" top="6084" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Current drawn from the USB supply while charging</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="6120" width="771" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The 2.2 A charging current corresponds to 0.65 C and gives a full charge in about 1.9 h. It is slightly above the 2 A maximum charge current of the cells, so a lower charging current would be preferable for the final design. A 5 V input would need to supply about 4.1 A for the full charging current.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
