    <region left="333" top="7488" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Safety factor of the screw terminals at the maximum battery current</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="7524" width="760" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> At full white brightness each strip would draw 3.6 A, which exceeds the 3 A JST-XH rating. With the brightness limited to 58% in software the strip current is 2.09 A, giving a safety factor of 1.44. The screw terminals carry the maximum battery current with a safety factor of 1.62.</p></content>
      </text>
