    <region left="333" top="8919" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Assumed worst-case clash force at the blade tip</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="8946" width="149" height="46" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">m.c</e>
          <e type="operand">F.c</e>
          <e type="operand">g</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">5.0968</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kg</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="333" top="8955" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Mass that would weigh the same as the clash force</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="8982" width="188" height="51" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">F.ratio</e>
          <e type="operand">F.c</e>
          <e type="operand">W.blade</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">21.8682</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="333" top="9000" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Clash force as a multiple of the blade weight</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="9036" width="763" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The clash force was not measured experimentally, so a 50 N transverse force was assumed for the structural analysis. This represents a severe impact condition and is approximately 21.8 times the blade weight, providing a conservative basis for the stress and deflection calculations.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="9117" width="178" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>2.2.3 Blade Loading Cases:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="9144" width="782" height="32" color="#000000" fontSize="8">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 8px;">//The blade is assessed under two loading conditions. Static loading represents the blade's own weight, while the clash case represents a transverse impact at the blade tip. The clash case is used as the main structural design condition.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="9198" width="94" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Static loading</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
