    <region left="333" top="10908" width="439" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Total tip deflection (clash plus self-weight)</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="10944" width="768" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The calculated tip deflection under the clash load is about 45% of the blade length, which is outside the small-deflection range for which the cantilever formula is valid, so the value is only indicative. It shows that a 50 N static tip load would bend the blade severely. In practice a clash is a short impact rather than a sustained static load, but blade stiffness (wall thickness or material) should be reviewed.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="11034" width="260" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
