    <region left="540" top="12132" width="430" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="8">
      <text lang="eng" width="430" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 8px;">//Tip force at which the lip bond reaches its strength</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="12240" width="762" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The lip bond has a factor of safety of 0.59 under the assumed 50 N clash load, so it is the weakest part of the blade connection. The bond reaches its strength at a tip force of about 29 N. Light clashes are therefore acceptable, but heavy duelling impacts could separate the blade mount from the hilt. A longer spigot into the hilt or a mechanical fastener would increase the strength.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="12303" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
