    <region left="349" top="12645" width="423" height="20" color="#000000" fontSize="10"><text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10"><content><p style="font-size: 8px;">//Blade surface temperature rise at the measured load</p></content></text></region><region left="0" top="12681" width="760" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The blade surface temperature rise is about 23 K at the 58% brightness limit and about 12 K at the measured load. With a 25 °C ambient this gives a maximum of about 48 °C, below the 80 °C maximum operating temperature of the WS2812B, so the aluminium heat-sink rod is not required.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
