    <region left="0" top="13500" width="765" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="760" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p><span style="font-weight: bold;">Conclusion:</span> The two vents remove about 0.36 W, roughly 11% of the 3.4 W produced by the converter at the measured load. The remaining heat passes through the hilt wall, giving an estimated internal temperature rise of about 8 K above ambient. The vents therefore assist the cooling, while the heatsink and hilt surface carry most of the heat. The measured temperatures in Table 5.3 verify this.</p></content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
</worksheet>